  "protocol": {
    "cohort": "All 1,482 windows in the four previously examined PINNS sites. Five 10 Hz observations span 0.4 s. Score top-mode ADE over 30 future steps and FDE at 3.0 s, in metres.",
    "quality_inputs": "Historical RTMPose features. q1 is the valid keypoint fraction (confidence >= 0.20); q2 is mean confidence over valid joints; q3 is mean relative annotated box height.",
    "proposal_section": "Section 5.3 of the original research proposal, conditions (1) through (3).",
    "proposal_clear": "q1 >= 0.85 AND q2 >= 0.60 AND q3 >= 0.08",
    "proposal_partial": "0.50 <= q1 < 0.85 OR (q1 >= 0.85 AND 0.40 <= q2 < 0.60 AND q3 >= 0.04)",
    "proposal_heavy": "q1 < 0.50 OR q2 < 0.40 OR q3 < 0.04",
    "archived_assignment": "Use src.data.features.assign_quality_bucket. Clear and heavy are disjoint. Heavy takes priority over literal partial in overlaps. All remaining non-clear, non-heavy windows are assigned partial, including those satisfying no literal rule.",
    "aggregation": "Equal window weight within each site and bucket. Give all four site means equal weight within each bucket. Paired differences are M1 minus M0; positive means higher M1 error. A clip can contribute windows to multiple buckets.",
    "interpretation": "Descriptive, conditional on four fixed sites and a single trained seed (42). Windows from a clip can be correlated. The buckets summarize estimated joint quality and image scale. Physical occlusion and blind-spot onset were not annotated in this analysis. No bucket-wise hypothesis test or five-seed inference was performed."
  },
